<title>SINGAPORE: Indonesia palm oil output at 11.7 mln T in 2005.</title>
<headline>Indonesia palm oil output at 11.7 mln T in 2005.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's palm oil output will more than double to 11.7 million tonnes by 2005 against about 5.6 million tonnes in 1997, the vice-chairman of the Indonesian Palm Oil Producers Association (GAPKI) said on Friday.</p>
<p>Derom Bangun said in a presentation to an edible oil markets conference in Singapore a sharp rise in the hectarage planted to palm will boost production. Plantings will increase to 4.6 million hectares in 2005 from 2.26 million hectares at present.</p>
</text>
